<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 11 March, from 1513 to 2020.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1513">1513 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">513 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Giovanni de' Medici proclaimed Pope Leo X</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorenzo-de-medici">Lorenzo the Magnificent</a> was announced as pope at 37. A lavish patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raphael">Raphael</a> and others, he promoted the indulgence campaign for St Peter's that provoked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> in 1517.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1702">1702 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">324 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Daily Courant, Britain's first daily newspaper, appears</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Published by Elizabeth Mallet near Fleet Street, the single-sheet Courant carried foreign news translated from continental papers. It ran until 1735, founding the British daily press.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1811">1811 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">215 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luddite machine-breaking begins in Nottinghamshire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a protest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nottingham">Nottingham</a> was dispersed, framework knitters broke dozens of stocking frames at Arnold. Attacks on machinery spread across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">Midlands</a> and North under the name of 'Ned Ludd'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-verdi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giuseppe-verdi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1851">1851 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">175 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Verdi's 'Rigoletto' premieres in Venice</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The opera of a hunchbacked jester was a triumph at La Fenice. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-verdi">Verdi</a> reportedly kept the aria 'La donna è mobile' secret until the final rehearsals, and it was soon sung in the streets.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1917">1917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British and Indian troops capture Baghdad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Stanley Maude's army entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> after the Ottoman garrison withdrew, avenging the surrender at Kut a year earlier. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> went on to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, under a League mandate.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1941">1941 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt signs the Lend-Lease Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The act allowed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> to lend or lease war supplies to nations whose defence was vital to America. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> received some 50 billion dollars of aid.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lend-lease">Lend-Lease</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1985">1985 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">41 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mikhail Gorbachev becomes Soviet leader</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 54-year-old Gorbachev was chosen General Secretary the day after Konstantin Chernenko's death. His policies of glasnost and perestroika unleashed forces that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1991.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2020">2020 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">6 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">WHO declares COVID-19 a pandemic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/world-health-organization">World Health Organization</a> described the coronavirus outbreak as a pandemic, with cases in over 100 countries. Lockdowns followed worldwide, and millions died in the years that followed.</p></div></li></ol>
